# Shell scripts must always check out with LF line endings, regardless of a
# contributor's local core.autocrlf setting, or bash chokes on the trailing
# \r baked into every line (e.g. "$'\r': command not found") when the script
# is run from a Windows checkout under WSL/git-bash. No .gitattributes file
# existed before this entry, so core.autocrlf=true (common on Windows) has
# silently reintroduced CRLF into native/ft8_lib_build/build_linux.sh on every
# fresh checkout, even after that file's LF-normalisation fix was committed
# during r1-sync-refiner-instrument-validation (see libft8.version.txt) --
# the fix only ever applied to the blob in that one working tree, not to any
# other checkout. Found and fixed during r2-coherent-llr-instrument (task 5.2)
# when the exact same failure recurred.
*.sh text eol=lf
